{
  "total": 141,
  "totalPage": 3,
  "page": 2,
  "pageSize": 50,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9c5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1945,
      "bookHadithIndex": 51,
      "text": "Abu Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"Allah has made some of your brothers as slaves under your care. So whoever has his brother under his care, then let him feed him from his food, and let him clothe him from his clothes. And do not give him a duty that he cannot bear, and if you give him a duty he cannot bear, then assist him with it",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1945-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1945-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1945-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1945-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9c6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1946,
      "bookHadithIndex": 52,
      "text": "Abu Bakr As-Siddiq narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"The one who treats his slaves badly will not enter paradise",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1946-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1946-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1946-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9c7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1947,
      "bookHadithIndex": 53,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that Abul-Qasim, the Prophet of Repentance, said :\"If somebody slanders his slave (by accusing him of committing illegal sexual intercourse) and the slave is innocent from what he says, Allah will impose the punishment upon him on the Day of Resurrection, unless it is as he said about him",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1947-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1947-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1947-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1947-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9c8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1948,
      "bookHadithIndex": 54,
      "text": "Abu Mas'ud [Al-Ansari] said:\"I was beating a slave of mine and I heard someone behind me saying: 'Beware O Abu Mas'ud! Beware O Abu Mas'ud!' So I turned around and saw that it was the Messenger of Allah. He said: 'Allah has more power over you than you do over him.\" Abu Mas'ud said: \"I have not beaten any slave of mine since then",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1948-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1948-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1948-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1948-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9c9",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1949,
      "bookHadithIndex": 55,
      "text": "Abdullah bin 'Umar narrated:\"A man came to the Prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! How many times should the servant be pardoned?' The Prophet was silent. Then he said: 'O Messenger of Allah! How many times should the servant be pardoned?' He said: ' Seventy times each day",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1949-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1949-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1949-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1949-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9ca",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1950,
      "bookHadithIndex": 56,
      "text": "Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"When one of you beats his servant then he (should) remember Allah and, withhold your hands",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1950-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1950-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1950-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1950-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9cb",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1951,
      "bookHadithIndex": 57,
      "text": "Jabir bin Sumurah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"That a man should discipline his son is better for him than to have given a Sa' in charity",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1951-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1951-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1951-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9cc",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1952,
      "bookHadithIndex": 58,
      "text": "Ayyub bin Musa narrated from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah said :\"There is no gift that a father gives his son more virtuous than good manners",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1952-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1952-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1952-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9cd",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1953,
      "bookHadithIndex": 59,
      "text": "Aishah narrated:\"The Prophet would accept gifts and he would give something in return",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1953-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1953-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1953-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1953-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9ce",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1954,
      "bookHadithIndex": 60,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"Whoever is not grateful to the people, he is not grateful to Allah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1954-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1954-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1954-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1954-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9cf",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1955,
      "bookHadithIndex": 61,
      "text": "Abu Sa'eed narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"Whoever is not grateful to the people, he is not grateful to Allah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1955-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1955-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1955-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9d0",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1956,
      "bookHadithIndex": 62,
      "text": "Abu Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"Your smiling in the face of your brother is charity, commanding good and forbidding evil is charity, your giving directions to a man lost in the land is charity for you. Your seeing for a man with bad sight is a charity for you, your removal of a rock, a thorn or a bone from the road is charity for you. Your pouring what remains from your bucket into the bucket of your brother is charity for you",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1956-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1956-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1956-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9d1",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1957,
      "bookHadithIndex": 63,
      "text": "Al-Bara bin Azib narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"Whoever gives someone some milk or silver, or guides him through a strait, then he will have the reward similar to freeing a slave",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1957-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1957-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1957-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1957-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9d2",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1958,
      "bookHadithIndex": 64,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"When a man was walking on the road, he found a thorny branch and removed it. Allah appreciated his action by forgiving him",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1958-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1958-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1958-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1958-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9d3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1959,
      "bookHadithIndex": 65,
      "text": "Jabir bin Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"When a man narrates a narration, then he looks around, then it is a trust",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1959-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1959-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1959-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1959-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9d4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1960,
      "bookHadithIndex": 66,
      "text": "Asma bint Abi Bakr said:\" O the Messenger of Allah! I have nothing except what was given to me by (my husband) Az-Zubair, shall I give it (in charity)?'\" It was said: \"Do not hold (your wealth) so that Allah will hold against you",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1960-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1960-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1960-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1960-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9d5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1961,
      "bookHadithIndex": 67,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet said:\"Generosity is close to Allah, close to Paradise, close to the people and far from the Fire. Stinginess is far from Allah, far from Paradise, far from the people and close to the Fire. The ignorant generous person, is more beloved to Allah than the worshiping stingy person",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1961-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1961-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1961-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9d6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1962,
      "bookHadithIndex": 68,
      "text": "Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Two traits are not combined in a believer: Stinginess and bad manners",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1962-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1962-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1962-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9d7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1963,
      "bookHadithIndex": 69,
      "text": "Abu Bakr As-Siddiq narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"The swindler, the stingy person, and the Mannan shall not enter Paradise",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1963-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1963-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1963-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9d8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1964,
      "bookHadithIndex": 70,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"The believer is naively noble and the stingy person is deceitfully treacherous",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1964-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1964-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1964-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9d9",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1965,
      "bookHadithIndex": 71,
      "text": "Abu Mas'ud Al-Ansari narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"A man's spending on his family is charity",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1965-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1965-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1965-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1965-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9da",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1966,
      "bookHadithIndex": 72,
      "text": "Thawban narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"The most virtuous of the Dinar is the Dinar spent by a man on his dependants, and the Dinar spent by a man on his beast in the Cause of Allah, and the Dinar spent by a man on his companions in the Cause of Allah.\" Abu Qilabah (one of the narrators) said: \" He began with the dependants.\" Then he said: \"And which man is greater in reward than a man who spends upon his depandants, having little ones by which Allah causes him to abstain (from the unlawful) and by which Allah enriches him",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1966-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1966-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1966-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1966-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9db",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1967,
      "bookHadithIndex": 73,
      "text": "Abu Shuraih Al-'Adawf said:\"My eyes saw the Messenger of Allah, and my ears heard him speaking when he was speaking and he said: 'Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, then let him honor his guest with his reward.' They said: 'What is the reward?' He said: ' A day and a night.' He said: 'And hospitality is for three days, whatever is beyond that is charity. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, then let him say what is good or keep silent",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1967-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1967-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1967-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1967-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9dc",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1968,
      "bookHadithIndex": 74,
      "text": "Abu Shuraih Al-Kabi narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:: \"Hospitality is for three days, and his reward is a day and a night, and whatever is spent on him after that is charity. And it is not lawful for him (the guest) to stay so long as to cause him harm",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1968-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1968-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1968-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1968-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9dd",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1969,
      "bookHadithIndex": 75,
      "text": "Safwan bin Sulaim narrated that the Prophet said:\"The one who looks after a widow and a poor person is like the Mujahid in the cause of Allah, or like the one who fasts all the day and stands (in prayer) all the night",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1969-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1969-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1969-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1969-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9de",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1970,
      "bookHadithIndex": 76,
      "text": "Jabir bin Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Every good is charity. Indeed among the good is to meet your brother with a smiling face, and to pour what is left in your bucket into the vessel of your brother",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1970-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1970-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1970-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1970-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9df",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1971,
      "bookHadithIndex": 77,
      "text": "Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Abide by truthfulness. For indeed truthfulness leads to righteousness. And indeed righteousness leads to Paradise. A man continues telling the truth and trying hard to tell the truth until he is recorded with Allah as a truthful person. Refrain from falsehood. For indeed falsehood leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire. A slave (of Allah) continues lying and trying hard to lie, until he is recorded with Allah as a liar",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1971-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1971-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1971-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1971-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9e0",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1972,
      "bookHadithIndex": 78,
      "text": "Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"When the slave (of Allah) lies, the angel goes a mile away from him because of the stench of what he has done.\"Yahya said: \"(I asked) 'Abdur-Rahim bin Harun if he approved of it,and he said 'Yes",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1972-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1972-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1972-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9e1",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1973,
      "bookHadithIndex": 79,
      "text": "Aishah narrated:\"There was no behavior more hated to the Messenger of Allah than lying. A man would lie in narrating something in the presence of the Prophet, and he would not be content until he knew that he had repented",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1973-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9e2",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1974,
      "bookHadithIndex": 80,
      "text": "Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Al-Fuhsh is not present in anything but it mars it, and Al-Haya' is not present in anything but it beautifies it",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1974-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1974-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1974-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9e3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1975,
      "bookHadithIndex": 81,
      "text": "Abdullah bin 'Amr said; \"The Messenger of Allah said:\"The best of you are those best in conduct.' And the Prophet was not one who was obscene, nor one who uttered obscenities",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1975-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1975-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1975-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1975-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9e4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1976,
      "bookHadithIndex": 82,
      "text": "Samurah bin Jundab narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Do not curse yourselves with Allah's curse, nor with His anger, nor with the Fire",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1976-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1976-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1976-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1976-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9e5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1977,
      "bookHadithIndex": 83,
      "text": "Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"The believer does not insult the honor of others, nor curse, nor commit Fahishah, nor is he foul",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1977-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1977-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1977-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1977-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9e6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1978,
      "bookHadithIndex": 84,
      "text": "Ibn 'Abbas narrated that a man cursed the wind in the presence of the Prophet, so he said:\"Do not curse the wind, for it is merely doing as ordered , and whoever curses something undeservingly, then the curse returns upon him",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1978-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1978-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1978-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9e7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1979,
      "bookHadithIndex": 85,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Learn enough about your lineage to facilitate keeping your ties of kinship. For indeed keeping the ties of kinship encourages affection among the relatives, increases the wealth, and increases the lifespan",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1979-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1979-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1979-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9e8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1980,
      "bookHadithIndex": 86,
      "text": "Abudullah bin 'Amr narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"No supplication is more readily responded to, than the supplication made for someone who is absent",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1980-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1980-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1980-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1980-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9e9",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1981,
      "bookHadithIndex": 87,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"(The burden of) what is said by the two who vilify each other is upon the one who initiated it, as long as the one who was wronged does not transgress",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1981-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1981-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1981-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1981-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9ea",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1982,
      "bookHadithIndex": 88,
      "text": "Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Do not vilify the dead (and) by that harm the living",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1982-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1982-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1982-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9eb",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1983,
      "bookHadithIndex": 89,
      "text": "Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Verbally abusing the Muslim is disobedience and fighting him is disbelief.\" Zubaid said:\"I said to Abu Wa'il: 'Did you hear it from 'Abdullah?' He said: 'Yes",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1983-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1983-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1983-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1983-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9ec",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1984,
      "bookHadithIndex": 90,
      "text": "Ali narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Indeed in Paradise there are chambers, whose outside can be seen from their inside, and their inside can be seen from their outside.\" A Bedouin stood and said : 'Who are they for, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"For those who speak well, feed others, fast regularly, and perform salat [for Allah] during the night while the people sleep",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1984-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1984-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1984-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9ed",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1985,
      "bookHadithIndex": 91,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"How wonderful it is for one of them that he obeys Allah and fulfills the rights of his master.\" Meaning the slave. And Ka'b said: \"Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1985-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1985-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1985-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1985-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9ee",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1986,
      "bookHadithIndex": 92,
      "text": "Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"There shall be upon dunes of musk- I think he said: On the Day of Judgment- a slave who fulfills Allah's right and the right of his patron (master), a man who leads a people (in prayer)) and they are pleased with him. And a man who calls for the five prayers during every day and night",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1986-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1986-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1986-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9ef",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1987,
      "bookHadithIndex": 93,
      "text": "Abu Dharr said:\"The Messenger of Allah said to me: 'Have Taqwa of Allah wherever you are, and follow an evil deed with a good one to wipe it out, and treat the people with good behavior",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1987-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1987-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1987-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1987-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9f0",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1988,
      "bookHadithIndex": 94,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Beware of Zann (suspicion), for indeed Zann is the falsest of speech",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1988-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1988-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1988-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1988-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9f1",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1989,
      "bookHadithIndex": 95,
      "text": "Anas narrated:\" The Messenger of Allah used to mingle with us such that he said to my younger brother: 'O Abu 'Umair! What did the Nughair do?",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1989-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1989-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1989-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1989-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9f2",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1990,
      "bookHadithIndex": 96,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated:\"They said: 'O Messenger of Allah! You joke with us?' He said: 'Indeed I do not say except what is true.'\" (Hasan)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1990-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1990-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1990-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1990-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9f3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1991,
      "bookHadithIndex": 97,
      "text": "Anas narrated:\"A man sought a mount from the Messenger of Allah who said: 'Indeed, I will let you ride on a she-camel's child.' So he said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What can ashe-camel's child do?' So the Messenger of Allah said: 'Are camels borne from other than she-camels?",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1991-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1991-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1991-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1991-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9f4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1992,
      "bookHadithIndex": 98,
      "text": "Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"O possessor of two ears!\" Mahmud said: \"Abu Usamah said: 'He only meant it as a joke",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1992-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1992-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1992-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9f5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1993,
      "bookHadithIndex": 99,
      "text": "Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Whoever avoids lying while he is doing so falsely, a house will be built for him on the skirts of Paradise. Whoever avoids arguing while he is in the right, a house will be built for him in its midst. And whoever has good character, a house will be built for him in its heights",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1993-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1993-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1993-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Batil"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1993-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9f6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1994,
      "bookHadithIndex": 100,
      "text": "Ibn Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"It is enough sin for you that you never stop disputing",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1994-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1994-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1994-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}